        <senderName>NWS Quad Cities IA IL</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 6 at 6:47PM CDT by NWS Quad Cities IA IL</headline>
        <description>At 644 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking slow-moving thunderstorms
along a line extending from near Swisher to Iowa City. Movement was
east at 10 mph.

HAZARD...Funnel clouds and brief heavy rain.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Ponding of water on roads and low lying areas.

Locations impacted include...
Iowa City, Coralville, North Liberty, Solon, Tiffin, Shueyville,
Oakdale, Lake Macbride State Park, Newport, Iowa City Municipal
Airport, Sugar Bottom Camp Ground, Cou Falls, Johnson County
Fairgrounds, Elmira, Morse, West Overlook, and University Of Iowa.

This includes the following highways...
Interstate 80 in Iowa between mile markers 239 and 252.
Interstate 380 between mile markers 1 and 11.
</description>
        <instruction>Conditions are favorable for the development of funnel clouds.  The
National Weather Service will continue to closely monitor the
situation, and may issue a Tornado Warning if the threat increases.
If you see a funnel cloud please seek shelter indoors and then
contact your local law enforcement agency for relay to the National
Weather Service.

If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
